// Closed records and the option-as-sum encoding.
//
// `#{label = value, ...}` builds a closed record (ADR-45; width and depth
// subtyping hold, so a record with more fields flows where fewer are
// expected). `record.get` / `record.insert` are the native field builtins.
//
// `record.get` returns an *option* -- and gandr encodes `Option A` as the sum
// `A + 1`, so a present field renders as `Inl(v)`. No separate Option type to
// retrofit later: the encoding is already compositional data.
def base = #{name = "gandr", stars = 1};

def extended = record.insert(base, "kind", "language");

record.get(extended, "kind")

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-last-value: Inl("language")
